            "text": "Implement the following plan:\n\n# Plan: AsyncRocksStore — In-Memory Reads + Async RocksDB Persistence\n\n## Context\n\nCurrent SALT storage backends have a trade-off:\n- **FlatFile**: Fast (reads from BTreeMap, I/O = 21ms/block) but not production-ready (全量内存, truncate overwrite, no crash recovery)\n- **RocksDB**: Production-ready but slow (delta = 105ms because reads hit RocksDB, I/O = 37ms synchronous)\n- **MDBX**: Slowest (I/O = 365ms/block)\n\nThe key insight: RocksDB's slowness comes from TWO sources:\n1. **Reads during delta phase** go through RocksDB (block cache + SST), 105ms vs FlatFile's 27ms\n2. **Writes are synchronous**, blocking the main loop for 37ms\n\nSolution: Create `AsyncRocksStore` that combines FlatFile's in-memory read speed with RocksDB's production-grade persistence, plus async background writes.\n\nExpected performance per block (Random scenario):\n- Current RocksDB: 250ms (prep 2.9 + delta 105 + root 103 + io 37)\n- AsyncRocksStore: ~120ms (prep 2.8 + delta 27 + root 86 + io 0 on critical path)\n- vs FlatFile sync: 145ms (prep 2.8 + delta 27 + root 90 + io 21)\n\n## Approach\n\nCreate a new `AsyncRocksStore` that:\n1. **Reads**: Served from in-memory `BTreeMap` (same as FlatFile/MemStore)\n2. **Writes**: Update in-memory state synchronously (microseconds), then send updates to a background thread that writes to RocksDB\n3. **Startup**: Load full state from RocksDB into memory (cold start recovery)\n4. **Shutdown**: Flush all pending writes before dropping\n\n## Files to Modify/Create\n\n### 1. Create: `crates/xlayer/salt/src/async_rocks_store.rs` (~300 lines)\n\nCore structure:\n```rust\npub struct AsyncRocksStore {\n    // In-memory state (reads go here — same as FlatFile)\n    state: RwLock\u003cStateStore\u003e,          // BTreeMap\u003cSaltKey, SaltValue\u003e + used_slots\n    trie: RwLock\u003cBTreeMap\u003cNodeId, CommitmentBytes\u003e\u003e,\n\n    // RocksDB handle (for background writes + cold start)\n    db: Arc\u003cDB\u003e,\n    _block_cache: Cache,\n\n    // Background writer channel\n    write_tx: Mutex\u003cOption\u003cstd::sync::mpsc::Sender\u003cWriteJob\u003e\u003e\u003e,\n    writer_handle: Mutex\u003cOption\u003cstd::thread::JoinHandle\u003c()\u003e\u003e\u003e,\n}\n\nenum WriteJob {\n    StateAndTrie { state: StateUpdates, trie: TrieUpdates },\n    Shutdown,\n}\n```\n\nKey methods:\n- `new(path)` → Open RocksDB, load full state into memory, spawn background writer thread\n- `load_from_rocksdb()` → Iterate CF_STATE + CF_TRIE, populate BTreeMaps (cold start)\n- `update_state(updates)` → Update in-memory BTreeMap synchronously, send to channel\n- `update_trie(updates)` → Update in-memory BTreeMap synchronously, send to channel\n- `update_state_and_trie(state, trie)` → Combined: update memory + send single WriteJob\n- `flush()` → Block until all pending writes complete (for graceful shutdown)\n- `impl Drop` → Send Shutdown job, join writer thread\n\nStateReader/TrieReader implementations: identical to FlatFile (read from BTreeMap).\n\nBackground writer thread:\n```rust\nfn writer_loop(db: Arc\u003cDB\u003e, rx: mpsc::Receiver\u003cWriteJob\u003e) {\n    for job in rx {\n        match job {\n            WriteJob::StateAndTrie { state, trie } =\u003e {\n                // Build WriteBatch, write to RocksDB (same logic as RocksSaltStore)\n                // No sync needed on every write — WAL provides crash safety\n            }\n            WriteJob::Shutdown =\u003e break,\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Modify: `crates/xlayer/salt/src/lib.rs`\n\nAdd `pub mod async_rocks_store;` export.\n\n### 3. Modify: `crates/xlayer/salt/benches/store_compare.rs`\n\nAdd `async_rocks` benchmark variant alongside existing mdbx/flat/rocksdb benchmarks. Reuse the same `run_*_blocks` pattern.\n\n### 4. Optionally modify: `crates/xlayer/salt/benches/block_io.rs`\n\nAdd `salt_async_rocks_32t` variant to the main block_io benchmark for a full comparison.\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n### In-memory StateStore (reuse FlatFile's pattern)\n```rust\nstruct StateStore {\n    kvs: BTreeMap\u003cSaltKey, SaltValue\u003e,\n    used_slots: HashMap\u003cBucketId, u64\u003e,\n}\n```\n\n### Cold Start (load_from_rocksdb)\n- Iterate CF_STATE with RocksDB full-scan iterator\n- Populate `kvs` BTreeMap + compute `used_slots` from data\n- Iterate CF_TRIE, populate trie BTreeMap\n- One-time cost on startup (seconds for 200K accounts, potentially minutes for mainnet)\n\n### Background Write Thread\n- Uses `std::sync::mpsc::channel` (no extra dependencies needed)\n- Writer thread receives `WriteJob` and builds RocksDB `WriteBatch`\n- Does NOT use `set_sync(true)` — WAL provides crash safety without forced fsync\n  (RocksDB WAL is fsynced by default on crash, `set_sync(true)` forces fsync per write which is expensive)\n- On `Drop`, sends `Shutdown` and joins the thread\n\n### WriteStats\n- `persist_duration` = time to update in-memory state (not disk time)\n- Add optional `async_queue_depth` for monitoring backpressure\n\n### Error Handling\n- Background write failures logged via `tracing::error!`\n- On drop, join the writer thread to surface any panics\n- If channel is full or disconnected, `update_*` returns error\n\n## Verification\n\n### 1. Unit Tests\n- Test basic read/write round-trip through AsyncRocksStore\n- Test cold start: write data, create new instance, verify reads\n- Test concurrent reads during background writes\n- Test graceful shutdown (flush pending writes)\n\n### 2. Benchmark\nRun `store_compare` benchmark with new `async_rocks` variant:\n```bash\ncargo bench --bench store_compare -p xlayer-salt 2\u003e\u00261 | tee /tmp/store_compare_async.txt\n```\n\nExpected results:\n- async_rocks delta: ~27ms (down from 105ms — reads from memory instead of RocksDB)\n- async_rocks I/O: ~0ms on critical path (down from 37ms — async)\n- async_rocks total: ~120ms/block (down from 250ms)\n- Should be close to FlatFile's 145ms or even faster (no sync write